// This is the main entry point for the React Native app when we use shadow-cljs to build the JS bundle.
// When we used Krell, the index file was generated by Krell itself.
// Krell build was used till OneKeePass Mobile v0.17.0

// RN Metro bundler looks for index.ios.autofill.extension..js as the entry point for ios autofill extension.

// --- iOS Autofill text-visibility workaround (facebook/react-native#54642) ---
// Under the New Architecture (Fabric, mandatory from RN 0.82), Paper-rendered
// text is INVISIBLE inside this app extension while layout/icons render fine.
// Root cause: in an `.appex`, RN's RCTSharedApplication() is nil, so
// RCTFontSizeMultiplier() returns 0.0. react-native-paper's <Text> applies an
// explicit themed lineHeight; with the default allowFontScaling=true that
// lineHeight is multiplied by 0 -> 0, and RN <Text>'s default `overflow:hidden`
// then clips the text to nothing. (Bare RN <Text>, which sets no lineHeight, is
// unaffected.) Setting allowFontScaling=false makes Fabric use a 1.0 multiplier.
//
// We patch react-native-paper (patches/, via patch-package) to default
// allowFontScaling=false ONLY when this global flag is set, so the change is
// scoped to this autofill bundle and the main app keeps dynamic-type scaling.
// Must be set BEFORE the app code loads, so we use require() (not hoisted) for
// the app below.
globalThis.__OKP_NO_FONT_SCALING__ = true;

// Load the ClojureScript autofill app AFTER the flag is set.
require('./src-cljs/cljs-ios-autofill-out/index.js');
